NC Digital builds custom ecommerce websites for South Wales businesses — online stores that look great, load fast, and make it easy for customers to buy. Every store we build is fully custom-designed around your brand, whether you're selling 10 products or 10,000.

Ecommerce sites start from **£800**, with the final price depending on the platform, number of products, and the functionality you need.

## Platforms we build on

We're not tied to one platform. We recommend the right tool for your business, then build a store that's designed specifically for you — not a tweaked template.

### Shopify

Shopify is our go-to for businesses that want a powerful, reliable store with minimal ongoing maintenance. It's ideal if you're selling physical products, need a fast checkout, or plan to scale. We design every Shopify store from scratch, tailored to your brand — no off-the-shelf themes.

**Best for:** Retail, product-based businesses, businesses planning to grow quickly.

### WooCommerce

WooCommerce runs on WordPress and gives you maximum flexibility. It's a strong choice if you already have a WordPress site, want full control over your store, or need custom functionality that Shopify's ecosystem doesn't cover. Like all our builds, every WooCommerce store is custom-designed to match your brand identity.

**Best for:** Businesses already on WordPress, those needing bespoke features, or service + product hybrid businesses.

### SureCart

SureCart is a modern ecommerce solution built for simplicity and speed. It's particularly well-suited for digital products, courses, subscriptions, and service-based businesses that want to take payments online without the overhead of a full product catalogue.

**Best for:** Digital products, subscriptions, coaching, downloadable content.

## What's included in every build

Every ecommerce site we build — regardless of platform — includes a fully custom design tailored to your brand. We don't use templates or pre-built themes. Your store is built from the ground up to reflect your products, your customers, and your visual identity.

- **Custom design** — built around your brand colours, fonts, and style
- **Mobile-first** — the majority of ecommerce traffic comes from phones; your store will look and work perfectly on every device
- **Fast loading** — speed directly affects conversions and Google rankings; we optimise every page
- **Secure checkout** — payment gateway integration (Stripe, PayPal, and others depending on platform)
- **Product management** — you'll be able to add, edit, and organise products yourself after launch
- **On-page SEO** — product pages, category pages, and metadata set up for search visibility from day one
- **Analytics & tracking** — Google Analytics and conversion tracking so you know what's selling and where your traffic comes from

## How much does an ecommerce website cost?

Ecommerce sites start from **£800**. The final price depends on:

- Which platform is right for your business
- The number of products and categories
- Any bespoke functionality (custom filters, booking integration, subscription billing, etc.)
- Whether you need us to set up and upload your product catalogue

We'll give you a clear, fixed price before any work starts — no surprise costs.

## A real example: AK Promotions

[AK Promotions](https://www.ak-promotions.co.uk/) is a South Wales events and promotions company whose website includes ecommerce functionality for selling event tickets directly through the site. NC Digital built and designed the site, and since launch it has generated over 2,800 visits and 75 enquiry form submissions — with no paid advertising. [See the full case study](/portfolio/ak-promotions/).

## Why choose NC Digital for your ecommerce site?

- **South Wales based** — local, direct communication throughout the project
- **No templates** — every store is designed for your brand and your products
- **All platforms, custom-built** — Shopify, WooCommerce, or SureCart, all designed from scratch
- **Honest pricing** — fixed quotes, no hidden fees
- **Post-launch support** — we're here after go-live, not just at handover

[Get in touch](/contact/) to discuss your ecommerce project, or [get a free website plan](/free-website-plan/) if you're still at the research stage.

